From 42c25ef22dd17e6509f5a2f22e3c0773862dc22b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:37:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Speed: IOP scheduler idle fast path, VU1 code image lookup by
 byte compare, game thread on the largest cores

- IOP kernel: thread state is written only through IopKernel::setState (a plain assignment no longer compiles),
  which keeps a ready count and a cached earliest Delay wake; beginNextReady returns at once when nothing is Ready
  and no delay expired, nextWakeCycle reads the cache. Timer deadlines bump a change counter on every write so
  nextEventCycle rescans only after one changed. GA2_IOP_CACHE_CHECK=1 checks every cached answer against a full
  scan (all IOP suites and a whole Eigou 1 battle: no difference). reset() rebuilds the list (and the cache).
- VU1: the last four code images are kept with their digests; a re-upload of one is matched by memcmp instead of
  a byte-wise FNV of 16 KB (3.9 % of the battle's game thread).
- The game thread pins itself to the cores with the highest kernel cpu_capacity on a mixed-core CPU (the Steam
  Frame's X4: battles 20-30 % faster than on its A720s); equal cores: unchanged. GA2_PIN_GAME=0 turns it off.

Desktop Eigou 1 battle: game thread 82 % -> 77 % at full speed; the heavy part holds 92-97 % speed (was 64-79 %).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
